  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "releaseNotes": "6.3.0 — No API change; the package now ships its XML documentation file and a buildTransitive props registering it as an AdditionalFiles input to the XML→OpenAPI source generator, so the response-envelope types (SuccessResponseModel<T>, ErrorResponseModel, ResponseModel, AppStatusCodes, etc.) document themselves in a consuming service's own OpenAPI document — .NET 10 discovers a ProjectReference's XML automatically, but not a package's. Bumped rather than repacking 6.2.0 in place, for the same NuGet-caching reason 3.1.0 records: 6.2.0 was already packed and published before this props file and XML doc file were added to its csproj, so a service restoring \"6.2.0\" from the feed silently gets the OLD package with neither asset. PREVIOUSLY, 6.2.0 — Additive + a mandatory-order rollout: adds PermissionClaimCodec (namespace Brainograph.Utilities.Authentication), a base64url bitset over the frozen ApplicationAdminPermission ordinals, and wires JwtAuthentication's OnTokenValidated to expand that single \"perms\" claim back into one ApplicationAdminPermission claim per grant, in memory, before any authorization filter runs. ClaimRequirementFilter, [HasPermission], User.HasPermission and bg-content's ArticleVisibility are UNCHANGED and keep matching the claim shape they already know. Motivation: tokens carried one claim per permission, so a SuperAdmin token was 5820 chars — it overflowed the 4096-byte browser cookie the dashboard stored it in (silently) and sat close to the 8 KB per-header proxy limit; the compact form is ~30 chars for all 174. Both wire formats are accepted, so old tokens keep working. DEPLOY ORDER IS MANDATORY: every service must be on 6.2.0 BEFORE bg-identity starts minting compact tokens, or permission checks fleet-wide see an empty grant set. No existing type changed; drop-in over 6.1.0. PREVIOUSLY, 6.1.0 — Additive: adds AppRoleNames (namespace Brainograph.Utilities.Models.EntityBase), the compile-time const mirror of the frozen AppAdminRole/AppUserRole names — one const per role plus AllAdmins (11-name CSV in enum order) and All (12 names: admins + User), for use in [Authorize(Roles = ...)], which accepts constants only. Also query-ready arrays: AllAdminNames / AllAdminNormalizedNames (11, ADMIN-ONLY — the admin gate) and AllNames / AllNormalizedNames (12, includes User — NOT an admin gate); plus UserNormalized (\"USER\") for EF NormalizedName predicates and Service, the S2S pseudo-role held deliberately outside the frozen enums. Pinned against the enums by AppRoleNamesTests. No existing type changed; drop-in over 6.0.0. PREVIOUSLY, 6.0.0 — Unified Users: audit actor columns (CreatedBy/ModifiedBy/DeletedBy) retyped bigint→Guid on IAuditableEntity and AuditableEntity<T>; adds PlatformIdentity (pinned uuid_v5 user-map namespace + Guid.Empty service principal). Epoch *At columns, entity PKs, enums, filters and the JWT surface unchanged.",
